[interviewer · RECOMMENDATION · 17:26] Now give me your recommendation to the CEO.

[candidate · 18:56] My recommendation: Brew and Bean should raise menu price, on a targeted basis, this quarter — that is the only lever big enough to close the gap.

The reason. Margin fall eighteen point, and COGS explain sixteen of it. Inside that, bean give 4.2 point and all other input give 11.8 point. So it is not a supplier problem, it is broad input inflation of roughly forty percent, and menu price has not moved in two year. Even perfect procurement cannot recover forty percent commodity move.

Sizing: to get COGS from 58 back to about 45 point, we need roughly twenty percent price increase. I would not do it flat — do it by item and by market, protect the entry drink, take more on the specialty and the alternative milk.

Risk: volume loss, since growth was all volume, not price. So I test in ten, twenty store first and measure elasticity.

Next step: two week price test, plus parallel procurement and waste workstream to capture five, six point more.
